  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "How many two-digit positive integers have at least one \\(7\\) as a digit?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\)",
    "B": "\\(18\\)",
    "C": "\\(19\\)",
    "D": "\\(20\\)",
    "E": "\\(30\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "A two-digit number containing a \\(7\\) must have it in the tens place or the ones place. There are \\(10\\) numbers with tens digit \\(7\\), namely \\(70\\) through \\(79\\). There are \\(9\\) two-digit numbers ending in \\(7\\), namely \\(17,27,\\ldots,97\\).\n\nThese groups include every eligible number, but \\(77\\) appears in both. It is the only overlap, so subtract one copy:\n\\[10+9-1=\\boxed{18}.\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
